    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance to help responders locate the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the single driveway entrance clearly on both sides so responders arriving under low-visibility conditions can identify it without delay.\n• Trim vegetation along the sides of the access drive so responders can move along it without obstruction.\n• Clear a designated turnaround area near the residence large enough for an emergency vehicle to reverse and exit without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Cut back dense vegetation growing close to the main residence and detached structure so responders can move around the buildings on foot.\n• Keep the vehicle parking area clear of parked vehicles along the path between the driveway and both structures so responders can reach either building directly.\n• Thin dense vegetation between the two structures to keep a clear walking path open for responders moving between them.\n• Post the property address visibly at the driveway entrance and again near the residence so responders can confirm they are at the correct location."
