    "recommendations": "• Trim tree branches that extend over or directly touch the house roof and walls.\n• Thin trees in clusters near the structure to create open gaps between individual trees.\n• Remove shrubs growing directly against the foundation and exterior walls.\n• Clear ground vegetation within several feet of the house on all sides.\n• Separate shrubs from nearby trees so fire cannot travel from low plants up into tree canopy.\n• Thin mixed vegetation on the sides of the driveway so vehicles can pass without obstruction.\n• Keep the full length of the driveway clear of overhanging branches low enough to block emergency vehicles.\n• Remove dead or dry ground cover that connects vegetation patches around the structure.\n• Clear vegetation along the rear of the property to allow movement around the back of the house.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so it is visible from the road, given the single access point and long approach.\n• Maintain a mowed or cleared strip along both edges of the driveway for its full length.\n• Thin trees scattered around the structure so none stand close enough to fall onto the house."
